  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the mean difference between outcomes and a reference value (5 Euros here), and preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. In this case, both lotteries yield a mean difference of 0, so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual did not mention any consideration of differences from a reference value, nor did they reference deviations or mean differences in their justification. Instead, their reasoning was based on risk aversion and conservatism. While the outcome of the decision reason is consistent with the individual’s choice (indifference), the process of reasoning differs. The individual did not use the mean difference rule as a basis for their decision. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
